{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhNXtga4dBNK8hJDd6Lm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `paginate` now returns every item on each page, including a final partial page.\n\n**Cause:** the end index in `src/pagination.ts:5` was computed as `start + pageSize - 1`, but `slice` already excludes its end index, so each full page lost its last item.\n\n**Change:** one line, the end index is now `Math.min(start + pageSize, items.length)`. The signature and validation are untouched.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm test` passes 4 of 4, but those tests only cover the empty collection, an out-of-range page and invalid arguments — none of them would have caught this bug.\n- I therefore ran a one-off check on a 7-item list with page size 3: pages 1–4 return `[1,2,3]`, `[4,5,6]`, `[7]`, `[]`. A page size equal to or larger than the list returns all 7 items, and page 7 at size 1 returns `[7]`.\n\nI did not add a regression test, since you asked for tests to be left alone; a page-boundary case in `test/pagination.test.ts` would be worth adding. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":394,"cache_read_input_tokens":8465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":394},"output_tokens":357,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18e9b156-c849-4a3c-a3cb-f9adda5bbbe5","uuid":"cdaf5b82-b96b-48aa-b5b5-193f05844124","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:41:37.559Z","request_id":"req_011CfhNXtRwXp1BBtwk8ba9x"}
